WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.660
Why would a cell make a protein all day, only to destroy it?

2
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.000
Most of your cells do exactly that with a protein called beta β-catenin.

3
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.920
Unless a signal tells them to stop, they destroy the free copies soon.

4
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.560
That looks like waste.

5
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.080
It is a design.

6
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.593
Picture a bathtub with the tap running and the drain open.

7
00:00:22.113 --> 00:00:23.833
The water level depends on both.

8
00:00:24.573 --> 00:00:28.973
The steady level of beta β-catenin is its rate of synthesis divided by its rate

9
00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:30.253
constant of destruction.

10
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:36.133
Slow the destruction ten-fold, and the level rises ten-fold, with no change in how

11
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.393
fast the protein is made.

12
00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:40.083
Take a cell that receives no signal.

13
00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:45.343
Every free copy of beta β-catenin meets the destruction complex, where the scaffold

14
00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:47.743
Axin holds two kinases beside it.

15
00:00:48.503 --> 00:00:54.663
CK1 puts a phosphate on serine 45, which primes GSK3 to add three more.

16
00:00:55.123 --> 00:01:01.503
A protein called beta β-TrCP reads the phosphates on serines 33 and 37.

17
00:01:02.023 --> 00:01:08.063
It belongs to SCF, a ligase that adds a chain of ubiquitin, and the proteasome

18
00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:09.183
destroys the protein.

19
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:15.043
That signal is a Wnt, a protein that one cell secretes and a nearby cell reads.

20
00:01:15.543 --> 00:01:21.063
Its receptor is Frizzled, and Wnt brings it together with a partner, LRP5 or 6.

21
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:26.763
Frizzled recruits a protein called Dishevelled, and the tail of LRP6 is

22
00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:29.043
phosphorylated and then binds Axin.

23
00:01:29.523 --> 00:01:33.943
The destruction complex is pulled to the receptor, and there it stops delivering

24
00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:35.663
beta β-catenin to the ligase.

25
00:01:36.163 --> 00:01:41.123
How it is stopped is still argued, but newly made beta β-catenin survives and builds

26
00:01:41.123 --> 00:01:42.117
up.

27
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:47.737
In the nucleus, a protein called TCF binds the DNA of many Wnt target genes, often

28
00:01:47.737 --> 00:01:48.957
before a signal comes.

29
00:01:49.477 --> 00:01:54.677
Without beta β-catenin, TCF holds a co -repressor called Groucho and keeps those

30
00:01:54.677 --> 00:02:00.117
genes off. In the simple model, beta β-catenin enters the nucleus, pushes Groucho

31
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:02.937
off and brings in the proteins that start transcription.

32
00:02:03.477 --> 00:02:06.777
So TCF turns from a repressor into an activator.

33
00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.587
Without a signal, the drain stays open and the level stays low.

34
00:02:11.307 --> 00:02:14.027
With Wnt, the drain is plugged and the level rises.

35
00:02:15.087 --> 00:02:17.887
The control is on destruction, not on synthesis.

36
00:02:18.727 --> 00:02:22.867
A protein that is always made and always destroyed can be raised by one move.

37
00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:24.547
Stop the destruction.
